<title>BELGIUM: EU says seals telecoms equipment deal with Korea.</title>
<headline>EU says seals telecoms equipment deal with Korea.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Monday it had reached a deal with South Korea that will open up the Korean telecommunications equipment market to European suppliers.  </p>
<p>&quot;European companies will now be treated as fairly as their Korean counterparts when bidding for contracts to supply telecoms equipment to the network run by Korea Telecom,&quot; the Commission said in a statement.</p>
<p>It added that Korean suppliers would also be &quot;treated equally when bidding for contracts in Europe's $22-billion- a-year market.&quot; South Korea's telecoms market is worth $6 billion annually.</p>
<p>The deal will now be submitted to EU ministers for approval.</p>
</text>
